I know this has nothing to do with TFA, just want to check my understanding of C. Doesn't the code example have a bug?
miniprintf(char fmt[], int val[])
{
int i = 0;
while( *fmt != '\0' ) {
if( *fmt != '%' )
putchar(*fmt);
else
switch(*++fmt) {
case 'd' : putint(val[i++]); break;
case '%' : putchar('%');     break;
default  : prterror(*fmt);   break;
}
fmt++;
}
}
If the static string was "%", the else branch would move past the end of the string. Assuming prterror doesn't crash the program, this reads out-of-bounds, right?
